## 5. Mascot direction

The mascots should be **fun, creative, intriguing, and memorable**. They should not be ordinary human characters.

Recommended direction: **stylized food creatures, abstract brand characters, or hybrid noodle/kitchen beings**.

Each mascot should express the persona’s relationship with Maggi, not merely look different.

### Mascot personality directions

| Persona | Mascot idea | Personality |
|---|---|---|
| Hostel Hungry | A monochrome noodle-cup student creature with headphones, a backpack, and a fork | Exhausted but resourceful, clever, always hungry |
| Maximalist Foodie | A chaotic chili-noodle character with mismatched features, flame hair, stickers, and bold patterns | Loud, experimental, expressive, playful |
| Practical Parent | A warm noodle-nest kitchen helper wearing an apron | Caring, dependable, calm, slightly busy |
| Conscious Upgrader | A calm noodle sprout or bowl character with leaves, grains, and balanced proportions | Mindful, fresh, composed, quietly optimistic |
| Midnight Recharger | A sleepy moon-faced noodle bowl whose steam becomes stars | Cozy, dreamy, gently humorous, comforting |
| Value-Stocking Homemaker | A dependable multipack-inspired pantry guardian character | Organized, practical, warm, efficient |
| Premium Flavor Explorer | A refined noodle character with chopsticks, global flavor accents, and editorial styling | Curious, sophisticated, adventurous, tasteful |

The mascots may be food creatures, abstract characters, or hybrid beings, but they must all feel part of one broader Maggi mascot universe.

## 6. Shared Maggi brand DNA

Even though each persona has its own visual world, all designs must retain recognizable Maggi brand DNA:

- Bold red and yellow brand energy.
- Warmth, appetite appeal, and comfort.
- The “2-minute” convenience idea.
- Noodle, bowl, steam, fork, chopstick, or packet motifs.
- A recognizable Maggi-inspired visual thread across all personas.
- Consistent mascot construction and illustration quality.
- A **seasoning-and-cube secondary prop family** so the system works in markets where Maggi is known for cubes and sauce, not only noodles.
- A subtle **Swiss red-and-yellow heritage thread** (early Maggi branding was built on this pairing).
- The shared **sachet** and the shared **"2" mark** in every persona world.
- A shared grid, spacing, and component system.

The goal is **one Maggi brand universe with seven distinct visual worlds**, not seven disconnected brands.

